    passageB1: `<p>More than a year ago, a Swedish teenager called Greta Thunberg was <strong>upset</strong> because politicians were not doing enough about climate change. Sweden had just had its hottest summer in over 250 years. So, Greta decided to <strong>take action</strong>. She stopped going to school and sat in front of the Swedish parliament with a sign that said "School strike for the climate".</p>
<p>Soon, other teenagers in different countries started doing the same thing. This grew into a big movement called Fridays for Future. These young people have brought new energy and a direct way of speaking to the climate <strong>discussion</strong>. They have also been very good at making politicians feel <strong>embarrassed</strong>.</p>
<p>On September 20th, they are asking adults all over the world to <strong>join</strong> them in protesting in the streets. If you work, own a business, or don't work, it's a good idea to think about what you can do to help.</p>
<p>This is a chance to show that different generations can work together on a problem that could cause <strong>conflict</strong> between them. Climate change affects everyone. We need to show that we know it will be too late if we only let young people <strong>deal with</strong> it.</p>
<p>Australia shows how people can be <strong>motivated</strong> to help. It was one of the first countries outside Sweden where young people started striking. Because of where Australia is on the Earth, Australians will be among the first to strike. There, a group of employers called Not Business As Usual has promised to support the strike. They will do this by closing their businesses, having days without meetings, allowing longer lunch breaks for people to go to protests, or simply making it clear that workers will not be <strong>punished</strong> for taking a few hours off.</p>
<p>In the UK, the Trades Union Congress has voted to support 30 minutes of action on that day. When the strike starts in America, more than 1000 workers at Amazon will also <strong>protest</strong>, as part of the Amazon Employees for Climate Justice campaign.</p>
<p>If you can't leave work, there are still many ways to help the strikers. You could give some of your money to a climate campaign, or write to schools, local newspapers, and politicians to support the protests.</p>
<p>Most of all, the young strikers want to see more people taking stronger climate action. The most helpful thing anyone can do is to look around, decide what needs to change, and <strong>promise</strong> to make that change happen.</p>
<p>This can't just be a 30-minute protest on September 20th. Climate change is not something we can simply win or lose. A climate scientist named Kate Marvel says it's like a slope we are sliding down.</p>
<p>The idea that we are <strong>doomed</strong> and there's no point in doing anything, is the last thing we need right now. We have already reached 1°C of global warming, but it's still not too late. We need everyone who cares about the future of the planet to take strong, <strong>consistent</strong> action. September 20th is the perfect time to show that you are one of those people. It’s time to <strong>take a stand</strong>.</p>`,
    translationB1: `<p>Bir yildan ko'proq vaqt oldin, Greta Tunberg ismli shvetsiyalik o'smir siyosatchilar iqlim o'zgarishi bo'yicha yetarli ish qilmayotganidan <strong>xafa</strong> edi. Shvetsiyada so'nggi 250 yildan ortiq vaqtdagi eng issiq yoz bo'lgandi. Shunday qilib, Greta <strong>chora ko'rishga</strong> qaror qildi. U maktabga borishni to'xtatdi va Shvetsiya parlamenti oldida "Iqlim uchun maktab tashlashi" degan yozuvli plakat bilan o'tirdi.</p>
<p>Tez orada boshqa mamlakatlardagi o'smirlar ham xuddi shunday ish qilishni boshladilar. Bu "Kelajak uchun juma kunlari" deb nomlangan katta harakatga aylandi. Bu yoshlar iqlim <strong>muhokamasiga</strong> yangi energiya va to'g'ridan-to'g'ri so'zlash uslubini olib kelishdi. Ular, shuningdek, siyosatchilarni <strong>uyaltirishda</strong> juda yaxshi bo'lishdi.</p>
<p>20-sentabr kuni ular butun dunyo bo'ylab kattalardan ko'chalarda namoyish o'tkazishda ularga <strong>qo'shilishni</strong> so'rashmoqda. Agar siz ishlasangiz, biznesingiz bo'lsa yoki ishlamasangiz, yordam berish uchun nima qilishingiz mumkinligi haqida o'ylab ko'rish yaxshi fikr.</p>
<p>Bu turli avlodlar ular o'rtasida <strong>nizoga</strong> sabab bo'lishi mumkin bo'lgan muammo ustida birgalikda ishlashi mumkinligini ko'rsatish uchun imkoniyat. Iqlim o'zgarishi hammaga ta'sir qiladi. Faqat yoshlarga <strong>hal qilishga</strong> qo'yib bersak, juda kech bo'lishini bilishimizni ko'rsatishimiz kerak.</p>
<p>Avstraliya odamlarning yordam berishga qanday <strong>rag'batlantirilishi</strong> mumkinligini ko'rsatadi. Bu Shvetsiyadan tashqaridagi yoshlar ish tashlashni boshlagan birinchi davlatlardan biri edi. Avstraliyaning Yer yuzida joylashgan o'rniga ko'ra, avstraliyaliklar birinchilardan bo'lib ish tashlashadi. U yerda "Odatdagidek biznes emas" deb nomlangan ish beruvchilar guruhi ish tashlashni qo'llab-quvvatlashga va'da berdi. Ular buni o'z bizneslarini yopish, uchrashuvlarsiz kunlar o'tkazish, odamlarga namoyishlarga borish uchun uzoqroq tushlik tanaffuslari berish yoki shunchaki ishchilarning bir necha soat dam olishi uchun <strong>jazolanmasligini</strong> aniq ko'rsatish orqali amalga oshiradilar.</p>
<p>Buyuk Britaniyada Kasaba uyushmalari kongressi o'sha kuni 30 daqiqalik harakatni qo'llab-quvvatlash uchun ovoz berdi. Amerikada ish tashlash boshlanganda, Amazonning 1000 dan ortiq ishchilari ham "Iqlim adolati uchun Amazon xodimlari" kampaniyasining bir qismi sifatida <strong>norozilik</strong> bildirishadi.</p>
<p>Agar siz ishdan ketolmasangiz, ish tashlashchilarga yordam berishning ko'plab usullari mavjud. Siz iqlim kampaniyasiga pulingizning bir qismini berishingiz yoki maktablarga, mahalliy gazetalarga va siyosatchilarga namoyishlarni qo'llab-quvvatlash uchun xat yozishingiz mumkin.</p>
<p>Eng muhimi, yosh ish tashlashchilar ko'proq odamlarning iqlim bo'yicha kuchliroq harakat qilishini ko'rishni xohlashadi. Har kim qilishi mumkin bo'lgan eng foydali narsa - atrofga qarash, nima o'zgarishi kerakligini hal qilish va o'sha o'zgarishni amalga oshirishga <strong>va'da berishdir</strong>.</p>
<p>Bu shunchaki 20-sentabr kuni 30 daqiqalik namoyish bo'lishi mumkin emas. Iqlim o'zgarishi shunchaki yutish yoki yutqazish mumkin bo'lgan narsa emas. Keyt Marvel ismli iqlimshunosning aytishicha, bu biz sirpanayotgan qiyalikka o'xshaydi.</p>
<p>Biz <strong>halok bo'lganmiz</strong> va hech narsa qilishning ma'nosi yo'q degan fikr - hozir bizga eng kerak bo'lmagan narsa. Biz allaqachon global isishning 1°C darajasiga yetdik, lekin hali ham kech emas. Sayyoramiz kelajagiga befarq bo'lmagan har bir kishi kuchli, <strong>izchil</strong> harakat qilishi kerak. 20-sentabr - siz o'sha odamlardan biri ekanligingizni ko'rsatish uchun ajoyib vaqt. <strong>O'z pozitsiyangizni bildirish</strong> vaqti keldi.</p>`,
