    passageB2: `<p>Just over a year ago, Greta Thunberg, a Swedish teenager, took a stand against the lack of action on climate change. After Sweden experienced its hottest summer in over 250 years, she decided to <strong>skip school</strong> and protest outside the Swedish parliament with a sign that read "School strike for the climate."</p>

<p>Soon, young people in other countries followed her example, creating the global Fridays for Future school strike movement. They have brought a fresh, direct, and <strong>compelling</strong> voice to the climate debate. They have also been remarkably successful at <strong>highlighting</strong> the failures of politicians.</p>

<p>On September 20th, they are asking adults worldwide to join them in protesting. Whether you are employed, an employer, or neither, it's important to consider how you can respond to their call. This is a chance to demonstrate <strong>solidarity</strong> and cooperation between generations on an issue that could easily divide them. Climate change affects everyone, and we need to show that leaving it to young people alone will mean action comes too late.</p>

<p>Australia provides an example of how support can be <strong>mobilized</strong>. It was one of the first countries outside Sweden where youth strikes began. Because of its geographical location, Australia will be among the first to strike. There, the Not Business As Usual coalition, made up of employers, has promised to support the strike. This support includes closing company offices, holding meeting-free days, allowing longer lunch breaks for protest attendance, or simply making it clear that employees won't be <strong>penalized</strong> for taking a few hours off.</p>

<p>In the UK, the Trades Union Congress has voted to support 30 minutes of <strong>collective action</strong> on the day. As the strike begins across the Atlantic, over 1000 Amazon employees will also strike, as part of the Amazon Employees for Climate Justice campaign, which has been going on for some time.</p>

<p>If you can't leave work, you can still support the strikers in other ways. You could donate part of your salary to a climate change campaign or write to schools, local newspapers, and politicians to support the protests. You can also <strong>raise awareness</strong> by sharing information on social media.</p>

<p>Above all, the young strikers want to see more people taking <strong>decisive</strong> climate action. The most helpful thing we can all do is assess the situation, identify what needs to change, and commit to making that change happen. This can involve <strong>adopting sustainable practices</strong> in your everyday life or <strong>lobbying</strong> for policy changes.</p>

<p>This effort cannot end with a 30-minute strike on September 20th. Climate change is not a problem we simply solve and then move on. As climate scientist Kate Marvel says, it's more like a <strong>slippery slope</strong>. We need continuous effort.</p>

<p>The kind of climate <strong>pessimism</strong> expressed by novelist Jonathan Franzen, suggesting that we are doomed so action is pointless, is the last thing we need right now. Even as we pass the 1°C global warming threshold, it is still not too late. <strong>Coordinated</strong>, sustained action from everyone who cares about the planet's future is essential. September 20th is the ideal opportunity to show where you stand and <strong>demonstrate your commitment</strong> to this cause. Don't miss the chance to <strong>make a difference</strong>!</p>`,
    translationB2: `<p>Xuddi bir yil oldin, shved oʻsmiri Greta Tunberg iqlim oʻzgarishiga qarshi yetarli choralar koʻrilmayotganiga e’tiroz bildirdi. Shvetsiyada 250 yildan ortiq vaqt ichida eng issiq yoz kuzatilgandan soʻng, u <strong>maktabni qoldirib</strong>, Shvetsiya parlamenti oldida "Iqlim uchun maktab ish tashlashi" degan yozuvli plakat bilan norozilik bildirishga qaror qildi.</p>

<p>Tez orada boshqa mamlakatlardagi yoshlar ham uning namunasiga ergashib, Fridays for Future global maktab ish tashlashi harakatini yaratdilar. Ular iqlim boʻyicha bahslarga yangi, bevosita va <strong>ta’sirchan</strong> ovoz olib keldilar. Ular, shuningdek, siyosatchilarning xatolarini <strong>ta’kidlashda</strong> juda muvaffaqiyatli boʻlishdi.</p>

<p>20-sentabr kuni ular butun dunyo boʻylab kattalarni norozilik bildirishda ularga qoʻshilishga chaqirmoqda. Ishlasangiz ham, ish beruvchi boʻlsangiz ham, yoki hech qaysisi boʻlmasangiz ham, ularning chaqirigʻiga qanday javob berishingiz mumkinligini koʻrib chiqish muhim. Bu avlodlar oʻrtasida ularni osonlik bilan ajratib qoʻyishi mumkin boʻlgan masalada <strong>birdamlik</strong> va hamkorlikni namoyish etish imkoniyatidir. Iqlim oʻzgarishi hammaga ta’sir qiladi va biz buni faqat yoshlarga qoldirish harakatning juda kech kelishini anglatishini koʻrsatishimiz kerak.</p>

<p>Avstraliya yordamni qanday <strong>safarlashtirish</strong> mumkinligiga misol boʻla oladi. Bu Shvetsiyadan tashqari yoshlar ish tashlashlari boshlangan birinchi davlatlardan biri edi. Geografik joylashuvi tufayli Avstraliya birinchilardan boʻlib ish tashlaydi. U yerda ish beruvchilardan tashkil topgan Not Business As Usual koalitsiyasi ish tashlashni qoʻllab-quvvatlashga va’da berdi. Bu qoʻllab-quvvatlash kompaniya ofislarini yopishni, uchrashuvsiz kunlarni oʻtkazishni, norozilik namoyishlarida qatnashish uchun tushlik tanaffuslarini uzaytirishni yoki shunchaki xodimlarning bir necha soat dam olishlari uchun <strong>jazolanmasligini</strong> aniqlashtirishni oʻz ichiga oladi.</p>

<p>Buyuk Britaniyada Trades Union Congress oʻsha kuni 30 daqiqalik <strong>jamoaviy harakatni</strong> qoʻllab-quvvatlash uchun ovoz berdi. Ish tashlash Atlantika okeani boʻylab boshlanar ekan, Amazon’ning 1000 dan ortiq xodimi ham Amazon Employees for Climate Justice kampaniyasi doirasida ish tashlaydi, bu kampaniya ancha vaqtdan beri davom etmoqda.</p>

<p>Agar siz ishni tashlab keta olmasangiz, ish tashlashchilarni boshqa yoʻllar bilan qoʻllab-quvvatlashingiz mumkin. Siz ish haqingizning bir qismini iqlim oʻzgarishi kampaniyasiga xayriya qilishingiz yoki maktablarga, mahalliy gazetalar va siyosatchilarga norozilik namoyishlarini qoʻllab-quvvatlash uchun xat yozishingiz mumkin. Shuningdek, ijtimoiy tarmoqlarda ma’lumot almashish orqali <strong>xabardorlikni oshirishingiz</strong> mumkin.</p>

<p>Eng muhimi, yosh ish tashlashchilar koʻproq odamlarning <strong>qat’iy</strong> iqlimiy harakatlarni amalga oshirishini koʻrishni xohlashadi. Biz hammamiz qiladigan eng foydali narsa - vaziyatni baholash, nima oʻzgarishi kerakligini aniqlash va oʻsha oʻzgarishni amalga oshirishga sodiq qolishdir. Bu sizning kundalik hayotingizda <strong>barqaror amaliyotlarni qabul qilishni</strong> yoki siyosat oʻzgarishi uchun <strong>lobbichilik qilishni</strong> oʻz ichiga olishi mumkin.</p>

<p>Bu harakat 20-sentabr kuni 30 daqiqalik ish tashlash bilan tugamasligi kerak. Iqlim oʻzgarishi shunchaki yechib, keyin davom etadigan muammo emas. Iqlimshunos Keyt Marvel aytganidek, bu koʻproq <strong>sirpanchiq qiyalikga</strong> oʻxshaydi. Biz doimiy harakat qilishimiz kerak.</p>

<p>Yozuvchi Jonatan Frannzen tomonidan ifodalangan iqlimiy <strong>tushkunlik</strong>, ya’ni bizning qismatimiz hal boʻlgani uchun harakat qilishning ma’nosi yoʻq degan fikr, hozir bizga eng kam kerak boʻlgan narsadir. Biz 1°C global isish chegarasidan oʻtayotgan boʻlsak ham, hali kech emas. Sayyoramiz kelajagiga befarq boʻlmagan har bir kishining <strong>muvofiqlashtirilgan</strong>, doimiy harakati juda muhim. 20-sentabr sizning pozitsiyangizni koʻrsatish va bu ishga <strong>sodiqligingizni namoyish etish</strong> uchun ideal imkoniyatdir. <strong>Oʻzgartirish kiritish</strong> imkoniyatini qoʻldan boy bermang!</p>`,
